 "_doc": "Characters of the dialog font glyph ids, the seed of the ROM extraction (tools/translate/font.py extract, tools/translate/dialog.py extract): the ROM holds glyph pixels, not the characters they show, so the reading of every glyph id is recorded here.  The extraction writes it into translate/<region>/glyphs/glyph_map.json, which is the single source of truth for every conversion and build afterwards (docs/formats/font.md).  `latin`: ids of the US / EU / DE font (the character table that used to live in src/common, plus the ellipsis and heart glyphs); `regions`: per release additions on top of `latin`; `jp`: Japanese font, first occurrence of each character only ($00B1 = full-width blank U+3000, $0270 = half-width blank, ASCII space); `jp_display`: readings of the Japanese glyph ids that repeat a character of `jp` - display only (worksheet reference text), the dialog converter keeps those ids as <XXXX> so that the conversion stays lossless.",
